muted"}><strong className={"font-semibold text-text"}>{"Signe Raaby"}</strong>{"Quality Bench Lead · 3 min read"}</span></div></div><ol className={"custom-glance grid grid-cols-4 gap-3.5 mt-11 max-lg:grid-cols-2"} data-anim-stagger={"70"}><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-1"}><span className={"custom-make-n tabular-nums [justify-self:start]"}>{"01"}</span><span>{"Wipe, don’t soak"}</span></a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-2"}><span className={"custom-make-n tabular-nums [justify-self:start]"}>{"02"}</span><span>{"Lift a ring with heat"}</span></a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-3"}><span className={"custom-make-n tabular-nums [justify-self:start]"}>{"03"}</span><span>{"Oil it each autumn"}</span></a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-4"}><span className={"custom-make-n tabular-nums [justify-self:start]"}>{"04"}</span><span>{"Mind the sun and the radiator"}</span></a></li></ol></div></section><div><nav className={"page-nav"} data-page-nav={""} aria-label={"Guide contents"}><div className={"container page-nav-inner"}><a href={"#step-1"} className={"page-nav-link is-active"}>{"01 · Every day"}</a><a href={"#step-2"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"02 · Rings"}</a><a href={"#step-3"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"03 · Oiling"}</a><a href={"#step-4"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"04 · Placement"}</a><a href={"#checklist"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"Checklist"}</a></div></nav><article className={"article-body custom-article py-16 md:py-24"}><p className={"text-[1.25rem] leading-[1.6] text-text"}>{"Solid oak is forgiving. It dents and scratches like any real wood, and that is part of why people keep it for decades: a scratch in an oiled top can be rubbed out, a lacquered one has to be stripped. Here is everything our bench does to the floor samples at the studio, and all you will ever need to do at home."}</p><h2 id={"step-1"} className={"page-nav-section font-medium"}><span className={"custom-kicker mb-2 block"}>{"Step 01"}</span>{"Wipe, don’t soak"}</h2><p>{"A cloth wrung out in warm water with a drop of mild soap is all a table needs day to day. Wipe along the grain, then dry it with a second cloth. Skip sprays with silicone or ammonia; they build a film that the oil can’t get through later."}</p><div className={"article-offset"}><figure><div className={"img-frame img-frame-rounded aspect-[4/3]"}><img className={"h-full w-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/856x1141.svg"} alt={"A light oak dining table set for two with stoneware bowls and folded linen napkins"} width={"856"} height={"1141"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></div></figure><p className={"article-note"}><b>{"From the bench"}</b>{"Linen napkins and stoneware are kind to oak. Hot pans and wet glass are not: use a board and coasters."}</p></div><h2 id={"step-2"} className={"page-nav-section font-medium"}><span className={"custom-kicker mb-2 block"}>{"Step 02"}</span>{"Lift a ring with heat"}</h2><p>{"A pale ring from a wet glass is moisture trapped in the finish, not damage. Lay a cotton tea towel over it and press a warm iron, no steam, for ten seconds at a time. The ring fades as the water lifts. A dark ring has reached the wood: a light sand and a coat of oil sorts it out."}</p><ul><li>{"Work with the iron moving, never resting."}</li><li>{"Check after every ten seconds; stop as soon as it fades."}</li><li>{"Finish with a thin coat of oil on that spot."}</li></ul><h2 id={"step-3"} className={"page-nav-section font-medium"}><span className={"custom-kicker mb-2 block"}>{"Step 03"}</span>{"Oil it each autumn"}</h2><p>{"Once a year, when the heating comes on and the air dries out, give every top a coat of hard-wax oil. Clean it, let it dry, rub a thin layer in with a lint-free cloth along the grain, wait fifteen minutes and buff away everything the wood hasn’t taken. Leave it overnight before you put anything back."}</p><div className={"article-offset article-offset--right"}><figure><div className={"img-frame img-frame-rounded aspect-[4/3]"}><img className={"h-full w-full object-cover object-[50%_45%]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/900x1200.svg"} alt={"The rounded corner of a light oak table with a small bottle of oil and a folded linen cloth"} width={"900"} height={"1200"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></div></figure><p className={"article-note"}><b>{"Less is more"}</b>{"A teaspoon of oil covers a coffee table. Too much stays tacky; buff until the cloth slides."}</p></div><div className={"alert alert-lg alert-primary"}><i className={"ph-light ph-drop alert-icon"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><p className={"alert-content"}><strong>{"Free with every oak piece."}</strong>{" A 100 ml jar of our hard-wax oil and a lint-free cloth come in the box. Run out? The studio refills it for free."}</p></div><h2 id={"step-4"} className={"page-nav-section font-medium"}><span className={"custom-kicker mb-2 block"}>{"Step 04"}</span>{"Mind the sun and the radiator"}</h2><p>{"Light oak deepens to honey in strong sun over a year or two; move lamps, vases and placemats now and then so it colours evenly. Keep pieces a hand’s width from radiators and vents. Denver air is dry, and oak likes to stay between 40 and 60% humidity."}</p><div id={"checklist"} className={"page-nav-section custom-checklist p-[clamp(1.75rem,3vw,2.25rem)] text-white bg-(--color-secondary-base) rounded-(--custom-r)"} x-data={"{ done: 0, total: 6 }"}><div className={"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4"}><div><p className={"custom-kicker"}>{"Each Autumn"}</p><p className={"custom-tab-title mt-2 text-white"}>{"The oak checklist"}</p></div><p className={"m-0 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-white/80"}><span x-text={"done"}>{"0"}</span>{" / 6 done"}</p></div><div className={"mt-5 h-1.5 overflow-hidden rounded-pill bg-white/10"}><div className={"h-full w-0 rounded-pill bg-primary transition-[width] duration-500"} {...{"x-bind:style": "`w